## Install

```bash
prog plugin install ./{{name}}
```

## Configure

Add to `.project/config.kdl`:

```kdl
plugins {
    {{name}} {
        // your config keys here
    }
}
```

## Hooks

This plugin reacts to:

- `on_issue_created` — fires when a new issue is created.

Add more hooks in `main.lua` and declare them in `.progit-plugin.json`.

## Capabilities

This plugin currently declares:

- `storage = true` — keeps state in `.progit/plugins/{{name}}/state.json`
- `network = false` — to enable outbound HTTP, set `network = true` and
  list allowed hosts in `network_allow`.

## Development

The SDK ships LuaCATS type stubs. Point your editor at them in
`.luarc.json` to get autocomplete and inline docs:

```json
{
  "Lua.workspace.library": ["../progit-plugin-sdk/stubs"],
  "Lua.diagnostics.globals": ["plugin", "context", "init"]
}
```
